HELPMENU {
[1;37mQuick start[0m
 [1;36mBehind a proxy[0m  In section 2 (telnet) or 6 (SSH), list your proxy and
                 set Trusted proxy only to YES, so only it is believed.
                 Block direct connections also turns away callers who
                 skip the proxy.
 [1;36mLimit per IP[0m    In section 1, set Connection limit to YES and Max
                 connections per IP.  Sections 3 and 4 are never limited.
 [1;36mGeoIP[0m           In section 5, set GeoIP lookups to YES; the defaults
                 need no API key.

 Pick a section, then a setting's number.  The whitelists show 10 entries
 a page: N and P turn the page, and any entry's number works from any
 page.  ? at a setting explains it; in a section, H and a number (H 2)
 explains that setting.  - clears a key, text or address.  X goes back
 one step.  Changes apply at once and are noted in the Audit Trail.
} T Quick-start help (H)


HCONLIM {
[1;37mN!SNTROWNUM. N!SNTROWNAME[0m
 YES: one IP address may have no more than Max connections per IP
 sessions logged on at once.  The Sysop (SYSOP or MASTER key), holders
 of the Limit bypass key and the addresses in the whitelists (sections
 3 and 4) are never limited.  A caller over the limit is shown why and
 disconnected.
} T Help: Connection limit


HMAXCON {
[1;37mN!SNTROWNUM. N!SNTROWNAME[0m
 The most sessions one IP address may have logged on at the same time.
 Used only when Connection limit is YES.
} T Help: Max connections per IP


HBYPASS {
[1;37mN!SNTROWNUM. N!SNTROWNAME[0m
